{title: 602 - O Brother, Be Faithful}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #602 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 602}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]O brother, be faithful! Soon Jesus [C/G]will come,
[G]For whom we [C]have waited so [D/A]long;
[G]O, soon we shall enter our glorious home,
[G]And join in the [C]conqueror’s song.
[G]O brother, be faithful! For [C]why [G]should we prove
[G]Unfaithful [D]to Him who hath shown
[G]Such deep, such [D7]unbounded [G]and infinite love—
[G]Who died to redeem us His own.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]O brother be faithful! the city [C/G]of gold,
[G]Prepared for [C]the good and the [D/A]blest,
[G]Is waiting its portals of pearl to unfold,
[G]And welcome thee [C]into thy rest.
[G]Then, brother be faithful! not [C]long [G]shall we stay
[G]In weariness [D]here, and forlorn,
[G]Time's dark [D7]night of [G]sorrow is wearing away,
[G]We haste to the glorious morn.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]O brother be faithful! He soon [C]will descend,
[G]Creation's omnipotent [D/A]King,
[G]While legions of angels His chariot attend,
[G]And palm wreaths, of [C]victory bring.
[G]O brother be faithful! and [C]soon [G]shalt thou hear
[G]They Savior [D]pronounce the glad word,
[G]Well done, faithful [D7]servant, [G]they title is clear,
[G]To enter the joy of thy Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O brother be faithful! eternity's [C/G]years
[G]Shall tell for [C]thy faithfulness [D/A]now,
[G]When bright smiles of gladness shall scatter thy tears,
[G]A coronet [C]gleam on thy brow.
[G]O brother be faithful! the [C]promise [G]is sure,
[G]That waits [D]for the faithful and tried;
[G]To reign with [D7]the ransomed, [G]immortal and pure,
[G]And ever with Jesus abide.
{end_of_verse}
